SUMMARY:Angel Investing 101
DTSTAMP:20260717T061415Z
DTSTART:20260721T173000Z
DESCRIPTION:Register here: https://luma.com/w1itcerp \nIn a world where onl
	y the very wealthy\, well connected\, and major institutions have access t
	o premium investment opportunities\, which have created massive wealth for
	 a small portion of the population\, the Innovation Center for Urban Entre
	preneurship team believes the key to closing income and wealth gaps global
	ly is to democratize access to opportunities across the investment ecosyst
	em. \nJoin the Innovation Center for Urban Entrepreneurship team for an ev
	ening of learning\, discussion and possibilities as we explore the basics 
	of angel investing and the role it plays in bringing new products and serv
	ices to market and the impact it has on wealth and job creation.. At this 
	event\, you’ll learn the key components to successfully navigate the criti
	cal-path of investing in private\, early-stage companies. \nThis session i
	s ideal for the following investment related stakeholders: \n\nProspective
	 Angel Investors who want to learn more about the world of Angel Investing
	\nInvestment Advisors (RIA/FA) who are looking for alternative investments
	 for their clients\nEntrepreneurs who want to learn more about what Angels
	 are looking for in their deals\nEntrepreneurs who want to meet/network wi
	th Angel Investors\n\nIon District Investor Activation Program: \nThe Hous
	ton Ion District Investor Activation Program along with Urban Capital Netw
	ork is helping build an equitable climatetech industry capable of rapid de
	ployment by addressing a fundamental challenge: the region’s lack of fundi
	ng for early-stage climatetech startups\, and especially for those led by 
	underrepresented founders. \nThis program from Greentown Labs and the Ion 
	brings early-stage investors from Greater Houston—a region playing a pivot
	al role in the energy transition—into the fold\, offering education on cli
	matetech investing\, channeling a pool of capital to young startups\, and 
	catalyzing a thriving climatetech investment ecosystem that prioritizes di
	versity\, equity\, and inclusion. \nIf you would like to join the program\
	, please fill out this form\, and if you have additional questions\, pleas
	e contact Juliana Bernal Martinez at jbernal@greentownlabs.com.\n\nhttps:/
	/iondistrict.com/event/angel-investing-101-8/\n\nFrom Ion District
URL:https://iondistrict.com/event/angel-investing-101-8/
LOCATION:Ion – Conference Room 029 – 030\, 4201 Main St\, Houston\, TX\, 77
	002\, United States
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ion-district
CATEGORIES:Ion District
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
